    <GaugingStation location="Newmilns" name="Irvine" number="83010">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">A flat v weir station to the East of Kilmarnock.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Weir superseded (Sep 1976) an unstable gravel bar control. Rating based on gaugings up to c.40 cumecs, a daily mean flow which has only been exceeded on 2 consecutive days in the record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Flat V weir within broad-crested flanks in a long straight reach. Stage data collected for this site dates back to 1959. Station added to peak flows dataset in September 2023 (WINFAP Files v12).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Sensibly natural flow regime.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Mostly upland catchment developed on basalts and metamorphosed sedimentary formations (mostly Carboniferous and ORS); extensively overlain by superficial deposits. Moorland and rough pasture predominate, significant afforestation in the north, mixed farming in the valley - Greenholm and Darvel are the largest settlements.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Flows contained in a well-defined channel and flood gaugings at 2.1m (measured at 65.2 cumecs) provides decent confidence in the flood estimation." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
